raised-in-apartheid-south-africa-2026-nobel-peace-prize-winner-navi-pillay-is-one-of-the-worlds-leading-human-rights-jurists-180989667/</guid></item><item><title>科学家从世界上最古老的乌龟身上采集了脸颊拭子。他的DNA可能揭示长寿的线索</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/scientists-took-a-cheek-swab-from-the-worlds-oldest-tortoise-his-dna-could-reveal-hints-to-longevity-180989663/</link><description>乔纳森是一只亚达伯拉象龟，大约 194 岁，是当今现存最古老的陆地动物。关于他的遗传学的发现可以为延长人类寿命提供线索</description><pubDate>Fri, 09 Oct 2026 17:28:10 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/scientists-took-a-cheek-swab-from-the-worlds-oldest-tortoise-his-dna-could-reveal-hints-to-longevity-180989663/</guid></item><item><title>这枚独一无二的青铜戒指让您可以一睹亚历山大灯塔的迷人风采，这是古代世界失落的奇迹</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/this-one-of-a-kind-bronze-ring-offers-a-tantalizing-glimpse-at-the-lighthouse-of-alexandria-a-lost-wonder-of-the-ancient-world-180989661/</link><description>埃及考古学家在安蒂罗多斯岛进行挖掘时发现了图章戒指，该岛曾经拥有一座奢华的托勒密宫殿</description><pubDate>Fri, 09 Oct 2026 15:21:52 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/this-one-of-a-kind-bronze-ring-offers-a-tantalizing-glimpse-at-the-lighthouse-of-alexandria-a-lost-wonder-of-the-ancient-world-180989661/</guid></item><item><title>一个世纪前，在建造狮身人面像的岩石中发现了一个已灭绝的鳄鱼头骨。事实证明，它属于一个新物种</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/a-century-ago-an-extinct-crocidilians-skull-was-found-in-the-rocks-that-built-the-sphinx-turns-out-it-belonged-to-a-new-species-180989641/</link><description>根据一项新的研究，该标本长期以来被贴错标签。古生物学家将其鉴定为一种此前未被描述过的鳄类属和种——鳄鱼和短吻鳄的近亲——他们以古埃及神荷鲁斯的名字命名。</description><pubDate>Fri, 09 Oct 2026 15:00:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/a-century-ago-an-extinct-crocidilians-skull-was-found-in-the-rocks-that-built-the-sphinx-turns-out-it-belonged-to-a-new-species-180989641/</guid></item><item><title>9月份的臭氧空洞是25年来最大的</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/septembers-ozone-hole-was-the-biggest-it-has-been-in-25-years-180989657/</link><description>平流层臭氧层空洞的大小每年都会发生变化，但上个月的空洞面积特别大，达到 1060 万平方英里。</description><pubDate>Fri, 09 Oct 2026 14:55:21 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/septembers-ozone-hole-was-the-biggest-it-has-been-in-25-years-180989657/</guid></item><item><title>由社区主导的苏格兰小岛上的考古发掘出土了一座具有“国际重要性”的中世纪修道院</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/a-community-led-archaeology-dig-on-a-tiny-scottish-isle-has-unearthed-a-medieval-monastery-of-international-importance-180989654/</link><description>该定居点由一位早期基督教圣人在 500 年代建立，“远远不仅仅是一座小岛上的教堂”。它在英国基督教化过程中发挥的作用可能比历史学家曾经意识到的更大</description><pubDate>Fri, 09 Oct 2026 14:35:25 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/a-community-led-archaeology-dig-on-a-tiny-scottish-isle-has-unearthed-a-medieval-monastery-of-international-importance-180989654/</guid></item><item><title>这些南美鸟类的声音可与手提钻震耳欲聋的声音相媲美，使它们成为世界上已知最响亮的鸟类之一</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/these-south-american-birds-can-match-a-jackhammers-ear-splitting-volume-making-them-some-of-the-worlds-loudest-known-avians-180989629/</link><description>裸喉钟鸟和红腿鸫可以发出超过 120 分贝的声音，这使它们与吹喇叭的大象或电锯相当</description><pubDate>Fri, 09 Oct 2026 13:00:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/these-south-american-birds-can-match-a-jackhammers-ear-splitting-volume-making-them-some-of-the-worlds-loudest-known-avians-180989629/</guid></item><item><title>德国考古学家在森林地面以下几英寸处出土了一座可能供奉战神火星的罗马神庙</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/just-inches-below-the-forest-floor-archaeologists-in-germany-unearthed-a-roman-temple-likely-dedicated-to-mars-the-god-of-war-180989650/</link><description>研究人员在卡珀斯堡堡垒附近挖掘时发现了该建筑的遗迹以及雕像碎片，卡珀斯堡堡垒是位于现代法兰克福郊区的古罗马军事防御工事</description><pubDate>Thu, 08 Oct 2026 19:32:02 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/just-inches-below-the-forest-floor-archaeologists-in-germany-unearthed-a-roman-temple-likely-dedicated-to-mars-the-god-of-war-180989650/</guid></item><item><title>JMW 特纳 (JMW Turner) 在近 200 年前绘制了这幅令人惊叹的罗马风景画。如果你仔细看，你还能看到他的指纹</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/jmw-turner-painted-this-breathtaking-roman-landscape-nearly-200-years-ago-if-you-look-closely-you-can-still-see-his-fingerprints-180989659/</link><description>这位浪漫主义画家于1830年代完成了《罗马，来自阿文丁山》。这件作品成为他 2014 年最昂贵的艺术品，预计 12 月的售价将再创纪录</description><pubDate>Thu, 08 Oct 2026 18:56:43 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/jmw-turner-painted-this-breathtaking-roman-landscape-nearly-200-years-ago-if-you-look-closely-you-can-still-see-his-fingerprints-180989659/</guid></item><item><title>使人类首次登月成为可能的软件工程师先驱玛格丽特·汉密尔顿 (Margaret Hamilton) 去世，享年 90 岁</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/margaret-hamilton-a-pioneering-software-engineer-who-made-the-first-human-moon-landing-possible-dies-at-90-180989653/</link><description>汉密尔顿普及了“软件工程师”一词，并创建了可以预测问题的计算机程序。她获得了总统自由勋章并入选国家航空名人堂</description><pubDate>Thu, 08 Oct 2026 18:42:32 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/margaret-hamilton-a-pioneering-software-engineer-who-made-the-first-human-moon-landing-possible-dies-at-90-180989653/</guid></item><item><title>加拿大诗人安妮·卡森将古代智慧带给现代观众。现在，她是诺贝尔文学奖获得者</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/canadian-poet-anne-carson-brings-ancient-wisdom-to-modern-audiences-now-shes-a-nobel-laureate-in-literature-180989655/</link><description>这位 76 岁的诗人、翻译家和散文家以其“大胆而富有创意”的方式将诗歌、散文及其之间的一切融为一体，从而形成了瑞典学院所说的“当代文学的新形式”。</description><pubDate>Thu, 08 Oct 2026 18:23:30 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/canadian-poet-anne-carson-brings-ancient-wisdom-to-modern-audiences-now-shes-a-nobel-laureate-in-literature-180989655/</guid></item><item><title>美国部分地区的流感季节提前开始，专家表示您应该考虑尽快接种季节性疫苗。以下是您需要了解的内容</title><